# Drafted by Gemini (side quests act 2 batch 1: quarantine), edited.

~ start
Narrator: Damp parchment leans across the mayor's desk like gravestones, smelling of boiled vinegar and wax.
wendel_somerton [weary]: Half the parish is coughing up centipedes in the taproom, yet I cannot bar the inn doors without three county seals in triplicate!
wendel_somerton [smile]: Would you take the sheaf to Miss Ledger and Miss Mayville for their stamps?
* We will fetch the seals -> accept
* Why triplicate? -> why
* Not now -> END

~ why
wendel_somerton [neutral]: One for the parish chest, one for the post bag, and one nailed to the Oak for the Green Queen.
wendel_somerton [weary]: Nobody remembers which magistrate wrote the statute, only that an unsealed plague is an unlawful plague.
-> start

~ accept
wendel_somerton [smile]: Bless your brisk boots! Do not smudge the ink in the fog, or Miss Ledger will make us start over.
quest quarantine_notices asked
set quarantine_asked
-> END

~ tamsin_seal
Narrator: Tamsin Ledger turns a page, her spectacles gleaming like brass coins.
tamsin_ledger [smile]: Form Seven-B, Emergency Pestilence and Bedstead Tally! I can countersign once we verify the active cots in the common room.
* [Medicine DC 10] Count the beds carefully -> count_ok | count_off
* Take her word for it -> count_ok

~ count_ok
tamsin_ledger [smile]: Fourteen feverish, three merely twitching, and two sharing a bolster. Everything reconciles to the half-column.
Narrator: Her iron stamp comes down with a crisp, joyful thud that rattles the inkwell.
set seal_tamsin
-> END

~ count_off
tamsin_ledger [sly]: Fifteen? The drover under the settle is only sleeping off turnip gin. I have struck him in red ink.
tamsin_ledger [smile]: There. Nothing warms the blood like a corrected ledger.
set seal_tamsin
-> END

~ post_seal
Narrator: Behind the wicket, Theodora Mayville sorts dead letters with a bone knife, her head tilting like a bird's.
theodora_mayville [neutral]: The quarantine circulars. Set them by the scale and do not breathe on the gum. I stamp notices after afternoon sorting.
* [Persuasion DC 13] Press her -> post_ok | post_stall
* [if flag.seal_tamsin] Show Tamsin's countersign -> post_ok
* [Deception DC 12] Forge the stamp -> forge_ok | forge_caught

~ post_ok
Narrator: With an unblinking stare, she drives the postmark into the wax with a sharp peck of her wrist.
theodora_mayville [angry]: Properly witnessed and weighed. Take your papers before you shed road grit into the pigeonholes.
set seal_post
-> END

~ post_stall
theodora_mayville [sly]: Haste ruins envelopes. Come back when the kettle cools and the dead letters are sorted.
-> post_seal

~ forge_ok
Narrator: While her back is turned, {name} inks a carved cork and presses three purple rings onto the parchment.
theodora_mayville [neutral]: Hmph. Still standing there? Keep your elbows off the blotter.
set seal_post
set quarantine_forged
-> END

~ forge_caught
Narrator: A gloved hand grabs {name}'s wrist as the fake stamp smears purple on the page.
doris_squire [angry]: Counterfeiting the postmark during a pestilence. Keep the smudged copy for the Mayor, and come to the cells until morning.
set seal_post
set quarantine_forged
jail wickermoor_constable_station:cells until days_since.jailed >= 1
-> END

~ file
Narrator: Wendel presses his brass signet into the wax and holds the three sheets up like prize squashes.
wendel_somerton [smile]: Three ribbons, nine stamps, and no blots! Now the village may be Deathly Ill in full compliance with the bylaws.
wendel_somerton [weary]: Take this for your shoe-leather, friends, and step lively around the inn porch.
quest quarantine_notices done
set quarantine_done
gold +25
-> END
